              { title: 'Not being organised', desc: 'Checking through guest arrivals, learning what to check for, and proactively communicating with guests if you are not sure about something will help you save time.' },
              { title: 'People Management', desc: 'When you first take over as a motel manager, you are the senior leader on-site, and developing your team is as important as your own checklist.' },
              { title: 'Cutting Rates', desc: 'New managers often reduce rates to fill rooms. The expression &ldquo;Bums in Beds&rdquo; is a classic and terrible saying for profitability. When you reduce your rates, you don&apos;t necessarily attract additional guests &mdash; you just reduce what the guests who do book end up paying.' },
              { title: 'Room Inspections', desc: 'You are accountable for the housekeeping standards. As cleaners complete rooms, you inspect them. Communicate directly with the staff member who cleaned the room if it is not to standard, and ask them to go back to fix the issue.' },
