          <div class="mt-6 border-l-4 border-[#4A554E] bg-[#F8FAFC] p-6 rounded-r-lg">
            <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-[#4A554E] uppercase tracking-widest mb-2">Tip</p>
            <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed m-0">When you first start, don&apos;t be too critical of the housekeeping staff &mdash; work with them to develop, help fix up some room issues, but still flag them to go back to rooms that are not to standard. Be calm, don&apos;t communicate negatively in front of the team &mdash; be direct with each staff member privately. When you address the whole team, make it about &ldquo;things to focus on&rdquo;, not &ldquo;you did this wrong, Cleaner A&rdquo;. Appreciate that when a new motel manager starts, the power dynamic in the motel is changing, and some staff may simply have built a strong relationship with the previous manager.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-5 space-y-5">
            {[
              { title: 'Ignoring preventative maintenance and deep cleaning', desc: 'On a spreadsheet, write down all of the rooms and tasks for cleaning and maintenance. Schedule out a plan over an extended period; sometimes you will need to shuffle tasks to fit in important issues that arise. Completing these tasks on a schedule will streamline your work and increase the motel&apos;s standards.' },
